{"skill":{"slug":"wechat-auto-reply","displayName":"wechat-auto-reply"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1771927239786,"changelog":"- Added official Homebrew installation guide and automatic dependency setup.\n- Switched usage examples and documentation from ./wechat-dm.sh to wechat-auto-reply global command.\n- Documented Homebrew skill file locations and configuration file path.\n- Included update and uninstall instructions for Homebrew installations.\n- Clarified that all dependencies will be installed automatically via Homebrew.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5950,"sha256":"1beddf0bcf0ba44dbde588c67eb6543c06a0d1ba8caddc796c1bd028d9610916","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1851,"sha256":"a028243eb93bb5fb86f40e247fec52297f2f311237c911b3a56cb0a5d9c23b61","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789082604823,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"0601c8ac9e6d15a3104e4690c3b46feb72e3a989a4c18eb35036366dd4a18465","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/0601c8ac9e6d15a3104e4690c3b46feb72e3a989a4c18eb35036366dd4a18465","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: wechat-auto-reply\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its reliance on powerful UI automation tools (`cliclick`, AppleScript's `System Events`) and screen content reading (OCR) for its functionality. While these capabilities are plausibly needed for automating WeChat, they grant extensive control over the user's desktop environment and can interact with other applications, posing a significant risk if the underlying skill code (not provided) were to be compromised or misused. The installation via a custom Homebrew tap also introduces a supply chain risk. There is no evidence of malicious prompt injection in `SKILL.md` or other clear malicious intent in the provided files.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779166727084},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":15,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789082604823},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This WeChat auto-reply skill is understandable in purpose, but it asks users to install unreviewed mutable code that can read chats and send messages automatically.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Screen capture, OCR, clipboard use, UI automation, and WeChat control are proportionate to this automation task, but they are sensitive macOS permissions with access to private chat content and outbound messaging.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The reviewed artifact is only SKILL.md and directs installation from an external Homebrew tap plus an unpinned pip dependency, so the executable behavior users install is not fixed or auditable from this package.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill scopes use to a named contact, but high-confidence replies are sent without per-message confirmation and the artifact does not clearly document whether chat content stays local or may be sent to an external AI service.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The install creates a global command and an OpenClaw skill link under the user's workspace, with uninstall steps documented; no launch agents, scheduled tasks, privilege escalation, or hidden persistence were found in the reviewed artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose matches the described capabilities: search a WeChat contact, OCR visible chat content, generate or choose a reply, and send it. Automatic sending for high-confidence replies is disclosed, but it affects private communications.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust the external Homebrew tap and are comfortable granting automation access that can inspect WeChat conversations and send messages. Review the installed formula/script before use, prefer confirmation mode for replies, and avoid using it on sensitive chats unless the data-processing path is clear.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: OCR of chat content and automatic reply sending are part of the stated purpose and are disclosed, but the privacy boundary for any AI processing is not clearly documented.\n[E3] expected: The cited command lists a specific OpenClaw skill installation directory, not broad home-directory reconnaissance or credential-path scanning, so this finding is downgraded.\n[T08] expected: Using Homebrew and pip is an expected install mechanism, but the external tap and unpinned dependency mean the reviewed package does not contain or pin the effective runtime code.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789082604823}}}}}